        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Karbala</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">10 October 680 (10 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muharram">Muharram</a> 61 AH)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Karbala, a desert plain about 70 kilometres north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a>, in modern-day southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The forces of the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a>, under Umar ibn Sa'd with the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ubayd-allah-ibn-ziyad">Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad</a> directing, an army of 4,000, which Shia sources say grew to 30,000; and a small party led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a>, whose companions numbered thirty-two horsemen and forty infantrymen in most accounts, and a few hundred in some</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">Husayn was killed with most of his family and close companions, and the surviving members of his family were taken captive to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a> and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>.</span></div>
